  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-1",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "CORE JOURNEY \u2014 read left to right, top to bottom.\nHome \u2192 Confirm \u2192 You & preference \u2192 Matchmaking \u2192 Match Found \u2192 Chat \u2192 Prompts \u2192 End Chat \u2192 Post-Shit."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-2",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "Direction \u2014 beige and brown.\nWarm paper ground, chocolate fills, a burnt-sienna highlight, clay for the other person. Cards lift off the page by a shade and a hairline. The UI plays it straight; the copy carries the joke.\n\nType: Bricolage Grotesque (display) \u00b7 Space Grotesk (UI) \u00b7 JetBrains Mono (timers, IDs, labels)."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-3",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 880,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Gender is set once at entry (screen 3) and then surfaces where it matters: as a filter chip on matchmaking, as a tag on the match card, and in the anonymous identity line in chat. Nothing else about a person is ever shown."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-4",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1880,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "SECONDARY \u2014 anonymous stats and the global board. Deliberately not a social profile: no photo, no followers, no bio, a one-tap new identity, and matching preference editable from here."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-5",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 1330,
      "text": "Alternates, low-fi. A is the original dark/lime treatment, kept for comparison. B trades the joke for clinical restraint. C goes full meme-poster \u2014 louder screenshots, harder to live in day to day."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-6",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": -960,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 880,
      "text": "THE MARK \u2014 the poo emoji redrawn as a proper mark: three dollops, a curled tip, eyes knocked out as transparent holes, no mouth. It replaces the placeholder swirl everywhere it appeared, and now leads the home screen."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "page-1"
  }
